## 6. Residual (not this cycle)

  These stay residual. They are not `[ ]` work unless the owner names one.
  Do not paste extra-backend lock lists here. Read SHIPPED.oot and run `ooda/scripts/*_smoke.oo`.
  Public first-machine install is `https://openooda.org/install.sh` (Linux x86_64). `ooda install` is the checkout XDG copy after you already have `ooda`. ARM / macOS / Windows packs stay residual.
  A human-in-the-loop product mode is not shipped. The human loop is `ooda fix`.
  vscode launches `ooda lsp`. `vscode/server/ooda-lsp.js` remains on disk and is residual.
  `qa/e2e/*.sh` and broken fixtures named in the `qa_master.oo` header stay residual. Run `qa_master.oo` for the product rail.
  Leftover: `import ".h"` still refuses. Do not treat `import_c` as proved from this board.
  AArch64 product-ELF dispatch is residual. Side emit-aarch64 hello/const-if assemble is a named lock. Link and qemu run stay residual.
  Extra emit-wasm and emit-x86 are not a complete backend. Dummy WASM `end` and IDENT leftovers stay dummy until a lock proves otherwise.
  Device GPU dispatch is residual. Hardware enclaves (SGX / TDX / SEV) are residual. Full general symbolic SMT is residual.
  Inventory door: `audit/library_status.oot`. Capability text audit: `scripts/audit_library_capabilities.oo`.

